actually responds to disruption and things like that, and that's the gap.

924
00:49:28.496 --> 00:49:28.506
Mm.

925
00:49:28.516 --> 00:49:32.436
And I really don't think that logoima is going to help us get any better with that.

926
00:49:34.056 --> 00:49:34.696
Cool. Dan.

927
00:49:34.956 --> 00:49:38.846
Thanks, Mr Chair. Ian, thanks to your organization, to your members for

928
00:49:38.976 --> 00:49:41.336
your input on the ports inquiry.

929
00:49:41.396 --> 00:49:41.636
Thank you.

930
00:49:41.726 --> 00:49:44.416
We're certainly hoping to complete that very soon.

931
00:49:46.056 --> 00:49:49.436
Just in your submission, you kind of paint a picture of

932
00:49:50.076 --> 00:49:52.456
the implications of this if it moves forward.

933
00:49:52.956 --> 00:49:56.496
I just wonder, if this moves forward, what impact will it have on the

934
00:49:56.536 --> 00:49:59.166
commercial or profitability of some ports?

935
00:49:59.196 --> 00:50:03.176
And of course, local councils rely on those ports

936
00:50:03.216 --> 00:50:07.176
to fund their operations. What does this bill

937
00:50:07.256 --> 00:50:10.096
have as an unintended consequence on port

938
00:50:10.736 --> 00:50:11.536
profitability?

939
00:50:11.546 --> 00:50:14.536
Yeah. I think there's three key parts to that.

940
00:50:14.576 --> 00:50:18.436
So like we've touched on the fact that there is an administrative cost to

941
00:50:18.456 --> 00:50:19.436
doing that.

942
00:50:20.436 --> 00:50:24.156
But that's only part of the story.

943
00:50:25.256 --> 00:50:29.096
Our ports, as you correctly said, there was a question about

944
00:50:29.116 --> 00:50:31.716
how certain rate payer funding going into the ports.

945
00:50:31.776 --> 00:50:33.556
No, the money flows the other way.

946
00:50:34.456 --> 00:50:35.696
It flows to

947
00:50:36.516 --> 00:50:39.676
their owners and help to keep rates down.

948
00:50:41.576 --> 00:50:45.276
So they are negotiating the ports with some of the

949
00:50:45.336 --> 00:50:47.576
biggest companies in the world, right?

950
00:50:47.646 --> 00:50:48.826
So let's take

951
00:50:50.036 --> 00:50:53.276
an international shipping line like Maersk, for example.

952
00:50:53.336 --> 00:50:56.876
Maersk earns more in two days than our largest port,

